@startuml seq_flt_oil_overtemp
title SC-FLT-07 - Oil overtemperature: fault lamp only

actor "Console user" as User
participant "Console" as Console
participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "TCU" as TCU
participant "Red LED\n(TCU board)" as LED

note over User, LED
Covers: SYS-FLT-006, SYS-FLT-008, SYS-HMI-001, SYS-SEN-003, SIM-PLT-007, SIM-CON-003
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
end note

note over TCU: control active, mode Normal, no other fault
alt oil heats up while driving
  Plant -> Plant : warm-up while driving (SIM-PLT-007)
else console forces the sensor voltage
  User -> Console : force OilTempVoltage (SIM-CON-003)
  Console -> Plant : sensor voltage forced
end
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Analog: OilTempVoltage of more than 130 degC
TCU -> TCU : oil temperature > 130 degC (SYS-SEN-003): oil overtemperature fault\n(FaultBits 11, DTC P0218-00) (SYS-FLT-006)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: FaultLamp = ON; gear and PCS_Duty unchanged
note right of TCU: warning only: no limit of gear or line pressure,\nmode stays Normal (SYS-FLT-006 note)
TCU -> LED : ON (SYS-HMI-001)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: Mode = 0 (Normal), FaultBits bit 11 = 1

... oil cools down ...
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Analog: oil temperature at or below 130 degC
TCU -> TCU : oil overtemperature fault cleared (SYS-FLT-008)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: FaultLamp = OFF (no other fault requires it, SYS-HMI-001)
TCU -> LED : OFF
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: FaultBits bit 11 = 0
@enduml
